    "rawResponseText": "A **hotel affiliation agreement** is a contract that lets a hotel operate under a brand or network while defining the rights, fees, standards, and obligations of the owner and the brand or affiliation group.[1][5][7]\n\nIn practice, the term is often used broadly to cover several **affiliation types** in the hotel sector, including **franchise agreements**, **management contracts**, **marketing consortia**, and **leasing contracts**.[1] Among these, a franchise agreement is the most common way for an owner to obtain brand affiliation: the owner gets permission to use the brand name, trademarks, systems, and often reservation or loyalty platforms, while paying ongoing fees and following brand standards.[3][4][5][6]\n\nKey points typically covered in a hotel affiliation agreement include:\n\n- **Brand use rights**: whether the hotel may use the franchisor’s name, marks, and systems.[3][5]\n- **Operational control**: whether the owner or an operator runs the hotel; franchise agreements usually keep control with the owner, while management agreements place operations with the manager.[3][8]\n- **Fees**: initial fees and ongoing royalties, marketing, reservation, and loyalty fees are common in franchise structures.[4][5][6]\n- **Standards and compliance**: required brand standards, property improvement plans, reporting, and audit rights.[3][5][8]\n- **Term and termination**: renewal rights, performance triggers, and exit obligations.[3][8]\n\nIf you want, I can also provide:\n- a **plain-English template outline** for a hotel affiliation agreement,\n- the **difference between franchise, management, and consortium agreements**, or\n- key **clauses to negotiate** before signing.",
